d #uuid "c0081fe2-ba7a-565b-921c-11dc8bd79c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447860} {:answer/id #uuid "fc911407-1e5d-58b7-8982-c859119fe356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0081fe2-ba7a-565b-921c-11dc8bd79c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447860} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b988c1-5329-5cf2-9e2b-7bef7867ab8c" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89286e95-724b-57e9-aee8-7d71e484cafb" :question/math-academy-id "q-107113" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $A={[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a,b\\in R}.$  \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $A$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $A,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & ka \\\\ kb & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "993ae900-0b4b-5abe-9f83-6751e2fb1c11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447862} {:answer/id #uuid "e695c7f1-667b-5020-86a7-e386d42f1a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e695c7f1-667b-5020-86a7-e386d42f1a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447863} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f0d1d52-7140-5348-9cd1-1a8686f2ba48" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448971} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c459fa0e-ba69-5797-a8f3-156380db3ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447864} {:answer/id #uuid "7a734cc8-b862-5978-9bf3-23c44c430045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a734cc8-b862-5978-9bf3-23c44c430045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447865} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0e53d6-ce03-554c-8ebc-cfddde79bc53" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a468ba0f-e58b-5475-abdf-a2e8beac6de7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447866} {:answer/id #uuid "8f7dce65-5e9c-54f3-bf6d-f0bdded38c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f7dce65-5e9c-54f3-bf6d-f0bdded38c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447867} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d468d9-ad9e-5842-b1a1-0d81106ec1a5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448973} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc820af5-3c85-57d4-81c4-43eca3e0a851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447868} {:answer/id #uuid "d8582ad8-c4ee-5cb2-b47f-96766390b92f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc820af5-3c85-57d4-81c4-43eca3e0a851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447868} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7cdbeab-101c-5f0b-8940-0a457a37d7f7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72b2f218-4463-5051-8c3b-5d02162b5905" :question/math-academy-id "q-107115" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$  and its subset $D$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices such that the sum of all its entries equals $0.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $D$ is closed under matrix addition\n\n- **II.** $D$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\n- **III.** $D$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\n- **IV.** $D$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Suppose ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1} & {d}_{1}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & {b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & {d}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $D.$  then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2} & {d}_{1}+{d}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n and since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({a}_{1}+{a}_{2})+({b}_{1}+{b}_{2})+({c}_{1}+{c}_{2})+({d}_{1}+{d}_{2}) & = \\\\ ({a}_{1}+{b}_{1}+{c}_{1}+{d}_{1})+({a}_{1}+{b}_{1}+{c}_{1}+{d}_{1}) & = \\\\ 0+0 & = \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe can conclude that ${A}_{1}+{A}_{2}$ also belongs to $D.$ So, $D$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, suppose $A=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\\in D$ and let $\\alpha \\in R.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\alpha A=[\\begin{aligned}\\alpha a & \\alpha b \\\\ \\alpha c & \\alpha d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n and so\nthe sum of the entries of $\\alpha A$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha a+\\alpha b+\\alpha c+\\alpha d & =\\alpha (a+b+c+d) \\\\  & =\\alpha \\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $D$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $D$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0eb038c-5b51-5d7c-bdf5-f61c5f197752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447870} {:answer/id #uuid "971fa534-d27a-5df8-a351-be678116035b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "971fa534-d27a-5df8-a351-be678116035b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447871} :answer-field/id #uuid "40fcbc27-f09e-5d13-b63b-a3bfac864c91" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448975} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ba547b1-a183-561a-904b-acf399df45c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447872} {:answer/id #uuid "3477959e-ae28-590c-8534-0de29bece5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3477959e-ae28-590c-8534-0de29bece5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447873} :answer-field/id #uuid "d27d2a30-f6b5-5889-b3e8-3a1ab661f5a8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448976} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d226a48-bc9a-5c4f-b777-3375deb35e36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447874} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd9c72e-2a23-5a4f-a198-740e3160f17e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bd9c72e-2a23-5a4f-a198-740e3160f17e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447875} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ab34820-b3b2-5e7d-b74b-405abb292421" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3976bf87-6856-55b9-92ed-31a90b18feea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447876} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f9c511-78a7-51fe-b700-8504529e7988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3976bf87-6856-55b9-92ed-31a90b18feea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447876} :answer-field/id #uuid "66584c33-4333-5200-8df1-e753f58cf7e7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3b977ec-88a0-5b97-96bf-4f197129ba2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-107119" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$  and its subset $T$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & c\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $T$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $T$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $T$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $T$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ 0 & {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ 0 & {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $T,$  then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ 0 & {c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nis also an element of $T.$ So, $T$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, if $A=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\\in T$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\alpha A=[\\begin{aligned}\\alpha a & \\alpha b \\\\ 0 & \\alpha c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nalso belongs to $T.$ So, $T$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $T$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2588e089-4786-5346-b42d-65c2740ae2ab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a48f3c2d-5d2d-5037-978e-ea63e6b65086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447878} {:answer/id #uuid "f7710f61-2737-5832-86aa-6c135c79edee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a48f3c2d-5d2d-5037-978e-ea63e6b65086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447878} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b256f02-33c3-5374-bdb1-42fe2fa2d4eb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448979} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "490b8b05-d48c-5b8c-b86f-40767d4b7e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447880} {:answer/id #uuid "79753851-ed7f-51cb-b5a1-99e169f34031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79753851-ed7f-51cb-b5a1-99e169f34031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447881} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad98e29-0528-562e-aab7-38e63a1efbfb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448980} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e8c8441-a2c1-5d8b-ac9b-5c23beabb8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447882} {:answer/id #uuid "5515c80a-9efb-5494-a89f-db172aa38284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e8c8441-a2c1-5d8b-ac9b-5c23beabb8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447882} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c426514-3859-57fd-a486-bab9ad75ab38" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "38344b2a-4c7e-5844-831c-94e852b34e5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-107131" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $2.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${0,1,t}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{2}[t]$\n- **II.** $2-t$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${0,1,t}$\n- **III.** ${0,1,t}$ is a basis of ${R}_{2}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1+0\\cdot t=0,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the first coefficient is nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent. In general, any set that contains a zero-vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n2-t=0\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot t.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32467c2c-5605-50e9-b961-a29535a0effb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d58913e0-0a2e-503b-895a-9e8a62183598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447884} {:answer/id #uuid "431ce8d2-3792-5889-8d11-0ad0193ca84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "431ce8d2-3792-5889-8d11-0ad0193ca84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447885} :answer-field/id #uuid "f788e45d-0eb5-52b3-a555-a20ba4a7e688" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448982} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "246df31b-44fb-5288-810d-e408e57f7633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447886} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8cf59f-c8d2-5114-8a53-9044ab7758d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "246df31b-44fb-5288-810d-e408e57f7633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447886} :answer-field/id #uuid "485057f3-721a-5540-bdfe-9c71b7bee298" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448983} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7efe3c0-c40d-5ad1-93ce-b169cedbc81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447888} {:answer/id #uuid "89361e74-53be-59dc-b7e9-2d650cec0404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89361e74-53be-59dc-b7e9-2d650cec0404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447889} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3e25578-3be1-5e27-a25b-8070d738ce2d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eace6f7a-724d-598c-b716-132ee8202185" :question/math-academy-id "q-107137" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** If $v$ is an eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =5$ then $v$ is also an eigenvector of the matrix ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{5}.$\n- **II.** An eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =6$ is also an eigenvector of the inverse ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the same eigenvalue $\\lambda =6.$\n- **III.** If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2,$ then $7v$ is also an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =2.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement is true. By the definition of an eigenvector, we have \n\n$$\nAv=5v.\n$$\n\n \nMultiplying it by ${A}^{-1}$ from the left, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=5{A}^{-1}v.\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $5$, we get \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}v=\\frac{1}{5}v.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $v$ is an eigenvector  of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\frac{1}{5}.$\n\n**Note:** In general, an eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to an eigenvalue $\\lambda $ is an eigenvector of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.$\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the statement above, an eigenvector of $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =6$ is an eigenvector of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{6}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(7v)=7Av=7(2v)=2(7v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(7v)=2(7v),$ and $7v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $7v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =2.$\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244032 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "083e9208-bad4-5d95-8617-a808610cfd9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447890} {:answer/id #uuid "e82608a8-5685-52b5-b9cd-f37053507f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e82608a8-5685-52b5-b9cd-f37053507f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447891} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae9dedb2-72df-5b77-917f-220b9a4e4d60" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448985} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8db24278-c96a-5a68-af63-c6a6368e9a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447892} {:answer/id #uuid "dbd30e1e-5645-5eaa-adf3-d528528c397e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbd30e1e-5645-5eaa-adf3-d528528c397e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447893} :answer-field/id #uuid "5606dc3a-9849-5dfb-b18a-a4377b645866" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448986} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74947044-d3b9-5c81-bb3b-1786caec1ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447894} {:answer/id #uuid "61b2ff36-6eee-584b-a567-1e35d3ce9ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61b2ff36-6eee-584b-a567-1e35d3ce9ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447895} :answer-field/id #uuid "fff9a238-82c2-5126-9f41-aac7f75ee83b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448987} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74a73409-a50b-5846-a8bf-f9fe458b594e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447896} {:answer/id #uuid "ec914062-c912-54b4-af4b-477d6aaf73ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74a73409-a50b-5846-a8bf-f9fe458b594e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447896} :answer-field/id #uuid "948b0716-db3d-59c5-a456-3c63914b24c4" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448988}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7a7e364-e908-54cb-a453-163231b198f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-107139" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $N$ containing all functions such that $f(0)=0.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $N$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $N$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $N$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- **IV.** $N$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, suppose $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are functions from $N.$ Then $f(x)=g(x)=0$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(0) & =f(0)+g(0) \\\\  & =0+0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $N$ is closed under function addition.\n\n- Statement II is true.  Indeed, suppose $f(x)\\in N$  and let $\\alpha \\in R.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\alpha f)(0) & =\\alpha \\cdot f(0) \\\\  & =\\alpha \\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $N$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $N$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8e680db-ef52-5417-81b7-6ffe9b4383d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447898} {:answer/id #uuid "19085411-2145-5329-9d1c-475729adfa8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8e680db-ef52-5417-81b7-6ffe9b4383d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447898} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b1197ba-c177-572c-bb95-f33fa8ad5099" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82cf67a9-3d8f-5ef6-a855-bb498bf43588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447900} {:answer/id #uuid "ae64a3e8-8b17-5d18-800a-c83f9d6df476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82cf67a9-3d8f-5ef6-a855-bb498bf43588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447900} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3c1736b-4604-5446-818c-f015abcb2042" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99d1af0d-a2b6-573e-97da-18a0ba798138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447902} {:answer/id #uuid "0672ccdf-f372-53ce-8a7f-559b6aa2d02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99d1af0d-a2b6-573e-97da-18a0ba798138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447902} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee0fabf2-df84-53f3-93cc-284ded8c1cc6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c2fad8-37dd-5870-9bbb-1b36235bf7bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447904} {:answer/id #uuid "164c2063-3e52-529b-8591-4a7fddde2578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "164c2063-3e52-529b-8591-4a7fddde2578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447905} :answer-field/id #uuid "2108e5a4-e8f2-5a2c-9c41-5db4f1dcbb80" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a3ebe5cf-3b69-5829-b6a6-d075f8831709" :question/math-academy-id "q-107141" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $W$ containing all polynomials of degree greater than $2.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $W$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $W$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $W$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- **IV.** $W$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{3}+1$ and $g(x)=-{x}^{3}+1,$ then\n\n$$\nf(x)+g(x)={x}^{3}+1+(-{x}^{3})+1=2,\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial of degree zero. So, $W$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{3}$ and $k=0,$ then\n\n$$\nkf(x)=0\\cdot {x}^{3}=0.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $W$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $W$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51114197-48b4-5104-bfb9-1476694d96da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447906} {:answer/id #uuid "76b7ee44-2461-590b-9754-2f59b1831440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76b7ee44-2461-590b-9754-2f59b1831440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447907} :answer-field/id #uuid "228f45e6-c374-52fd-9af8-a8ca562b3eb7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cc0ede9-e1c1-5c90-b6a3-9be6bdd5c841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447908} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3441cf-7ed5-523d-a20d-91318604e063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cc0ede9-e1c1-5c90-b6a3-9be6